The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```dts
reserved-memory {
	#address-cells = <1>;
	#size-cells = <1>;
	ranges;

	tee@10100000 {
		reg = <0x10100000 0xf00000>;
		no-map;
	};
};
```
Reason:
The `reserved-memory` node was incorrectly defined in the `rtd1295.dtsi` file rather than in the centralized `rtd129x.dtsi` file. This caused issues in the memory reservations for RPC regions specific to the Realtek RTD129x SoCs, potentially leading to improper memory management and access.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```dts
// Move reserved-memory node to RTD129x DT
reserved-memory {
	#address-cells = <1>;
	#size-cells = <1>;
	ranges;

	tee@10100000 {
		reg = <0x10100000 0xf00000>;
		no-map;
	};
};
```
Reason:
Moving the `reserved-memory` node to the `rtd129x.dtsi` file consolidates the memory reservation logic for the RTD129x SoCs, ensuring that RPC regions are properly reserved and accessible, thereby resolving the memory management issues introduced by the earlier incorrect placement.

